# Left over from the SQLite era, and kept as cheap insurance: hold.db is still on disk, and a
# copy of it inside an image would be both stale and a leak of whatever was saved when it was
# built.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# The ** matters. A bare `bin/` matches only the context root, so src/Hold/obj still came in —
# and obj/project.assets.json holds absolute Windows paths to the host's NuGet cache. Copied
# into a Linux image and reused by `publish --no-restore`, it fails inside ResolvePackageAssets
# with a stack trace that says nothing about the actual cause.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Tests are not published, and copying them only invalidates the build cache.
tests/

.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

Dockerfile
compose.yaml
render.yaml
.dockerignore
CLAUDE.md
*.md
